{
  "Displays items in a hierarchy. Rows can be expanded and collapsed, selected individually or in groups, and searched. Check boxes can roll up to parent rows, and children can load on demand when a row is first expanded. Large trees render only the visible rows.": "",
  "Items are objects with a `children` array, or with a `parentId` as described below. `value` is the key of the selected row, and `x-model` provides two-way binding. When you create the tree with `new`, fill and control it programmatically. Plain or reactive items changed in place appear after `refresh()`, or `refreshItem(key)` for a single row.": "",
  "File explorer with on-demand loading": "",
  "`loadChildren` loads the children of a row the first time it expands, and `hasChildren: false` marks a row with nothing to load. The row shows a busy state while loading. If loading fails, the row reports the error and offers a retry (“Shared” fails once in this example). `iconField` provides the icons, and here it is a function.": "",
  "`selectionMode` is `single` (the default), `multiple` or `none`. With `multiple`, Ctrl (⌘) + click adds or removes a row, Shift + click selects a range, and the keyboard follows the APG multi-select tree pattern.": "",
  "Check boxes in a permissions tree": "",
  "`showCheckBoxes` adds a check box to every row. Checking a parent checks its children, and a parent shows an indeterminate state while only some are checked (`checkRecursive`, on by default). `checkedKeys` sets and reports the checked rows, and Space toggles the focused one.": "",
  "Search and filtering": "",
  "`searchEnabled` adds a search box. Matches appear with their parents expanded, and clearing the search restores the previous state. `searchValue` or `filter(text)` filters programmatically, and `searchMode` is `contains` or `startswith`.": "",
  "Flat data, fields and templates": "Düz veri, field'lar ve şablonlar",
  "Flat rows reference their parent through `parentField`, which defaults to `parentId`. Any field can be a property name or a function. `itemTemplate` customizes a row's content, and `enabledField` and `expandedField` apply per row.": "",
  "Large trees": "Büyük ağaçlar",
  "Only expanded rows are rendered, and when more than `virtualFrom` (500) rows are on screen, only the visible ones are rendered. This example has 50 departments of 200 people, for 10,050 rows when fully expanded. Give the tree a height so that it scrolls internally.": "",
  "Sizes, connector lines and expand behavior": "",
  "Moves focus into the tree, to the focused row, the selected row or the first row, and out again. The tree is one Tab stop.": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous visible row.": "",
  "Expands a collapsed row, or moves to the first child of an expanded row. On right-to-left pages, use Left.": "",
  "Collapses an expanded row, or moves to the parent of a collapsed row. On right-to-left pages, use Right.": "",
  "Moves to the first or last row, or up or down by one page.": "",
  "Expands all siblings of the row.": "",
  "Moves to the next row whose text starts with that character. Type quickly to match a longer prefix.": "",
  "Selects the row, and with `multiple` selects only that row.": "",
  "Toggles the check box if shown. Otherwise, it selects the row, or toggles it with `multiple`.": "",
  "With `multiple`, moves and toggles the next row.": "",
  "With `multiple`, selects from the last selected row to the current row, up to the first or last row, or everything.": "",
  "Moves focus into the tree.": "",
  "`role=\"tree\"`, named by `label`, or by `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby` on the tag, with `aria-multiselectable` for `multiple`.": "",
  "`role=\"treeitem\"` with `aria-level`, `aria-setsize`, `aria-posinset`, `aria-expanded` on parents, `aria-selected` (unless `none`), `aria-checked` (`true`, `false`, `mixed`) with check boxes, and `aria-disabled`.": "",
  "An expanded row contains a `role=\"group\"` with its children. A large tree renders its rows flat, with the same levels and positions.": "",
  "A row loading its children has `aria-busy=\"true\"`, and a failed load is described by its message (`aria-describedby`).": "",
  "Roving `tabindex`, so one row is in the Tab order. The focus ring appears only during keyboard use.": "",
  "The tree has four strings, all from `uiLocale.strings`: `noItems` (empty tree), `loadFailed` and `retry` (failed load), and `search` (the search box).": "",
  "The root. `data-size`, `data-lines`, `data-checkboxes`, `data-windowed`, `data-empty`, `data-disabled`.": "Kök. `data-size`, `data-lines`, `data-checkboxes`, `data-windowed`, `data-empty`, `data-disabled`.",
  "The search box, the tree and the empty text.": "",
  "A row and its children: `data-selected`, `data-expanded`, `data-branch`, `data-state`, `data-loading`, `data-error`, `data-disabled` and `--_level`.": "",
  "The visible row.": "",
  "The children of an expanded row.": "",
  "A failed load and its retry button.": "Başarısız yükleme ve yeniden deneme düğmesi.",
  "Units: a row in each state (`hover`, `pressed`, `selected`, `selected-hover`, `focus`, `disabled`), the selection indicator, the expander and its plate, and the loading ring.": "",
  "Units: the check box (`hover`, `checked`, `checked-hover`, `disabled`, `checked-disabled`) and the other parts.": "Unit'ler: onay kutusu (`hover`, `checked`, `checked-hover`, `disabled`, `checked-disabled`) ve diğer parçalar.",
  "Sizes per size class, and the indent of each level.": "",
  "The space between two rows, and the expander plate the connector lines are centered under.": "",
  "The connector lines (`showLines`).": "",
  "Nested items with a `children` array, or flat items with a `parentId`. A function is tracked, and items changed in place appear after `refresh()`.": "",
  "A property name or a function `(item) => …`. An item without a key serves as its own key. `parentField`, or items with a `parentId`, makes the list flat.": "",
  "Per item: an icon, whether the row can be selected or checked, whether it starts expanded (changing this expands or collapses it), and whether it has children to load.": "",
  "Loads the children of a row when it is first expanded. The row shows a busy state meanwhile, and offers a retry if loading fails.": "",
  "How many rows can be selected.": "Kaç satırın seçilebileceği.",
  "The selected key (`single`) or keys (`multiple`). `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "The expanded rows. `onExpanded` and `onCollapsed` report changes made by the user.": "",
  "Adds a check box to every row.": "",
  "Checking a parent checks its children, and a parent is indeterminate when only some are checked.": "",
  "The checked rows. A parent is included when all its children are checked. `onCheckChanged` reports changes.": "",
  "Adds a search box at the top.": "",
  "How the search matches row text.": "",
  "The text used to filter rows. Matches appear with their parents expanded.": "",
  "What expands a branch, in addition to its expander and the keyboard.": "",
  "Draws connector lines from each parent to its children.": "",
  "The accessible name of the tree. `aria-label` and `aria-labelledby` on the tag also work.": "",
  "When more rows than this are on screen, only the visible rows are rendered.": "",
  "Customizes the content of a row.": "",
  "The selected or checked items, in tree order.": "",
  "The element with `role=\"tree\"`.": "`role=\"tree\"` öğesi.",
  "Expands or collapses a row, loading its children first if needed. The cancelable events run.": "",
  "Applies to every row whose children are known, with no event per row.": "",
  "Programmatic control. `select` adds to the selection with `multiple`.": "",
  "Programmatic control.": "",
  "Sets `searchValue`.": "`searchValue` atar.",
  "Expands the row's parents, scrolls it into view and sets focus on it.": "",
  "Reloads a row's children, or all loaded children when no key is given.": "",
  "Your items can be plain or reactive, and the tree reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. The items, their children, text and states are read again, and loaded children are kept.": "",
  "Redraws one row after its item changes in place, including its text, icon and state. Use `refresh()` for its children.": "",
  "The item with that key.": "O anahtarlı öğe.",
  "Sets focus on the row that Tab reaches.": "",
  "Occurs before a row expands or collapses. `e`: `{ item, key, byUser, cancel, source, event? }`. Set `e.cancel = true` to keep the current state.": "",
  "Occurs after a row expands or collapses. `e`: `{ item, key, byUser, source }`.": "",
  "`{ item, key, state, keys, byUser, source }`. `item` is `null` when several rows changed at once.": "",
  "Occurs when a row is clicked, or when Enter is pressed on it. `{ item, key, source, event }`": ""
